  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. We have only one multimodal data point, so we know nothing about whether the 'weighted' fusion strategy is actually responsible for the gain over the RNA-only baseline (0.653) or whether a simpler 'concat' fusion would perform comparably. Config_038 is identical to config_039 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, making it a clean single-variable A/B test. This is the highest-information next step: if concat matches weighted, fusion strategy is not a critical design axis and we can focus budget on other dimensions (e.g., image encoder, aggregation); if weighted clearly wins, we confirm that the learned fusion weights are important and should be preserved in all future multimodal experiments. This is preferred over testing avgpool (already shown ≈ transformer in RNA-only, configs 005/006) or image-only ViT-L (informative but less directly actionable for optimization)."
}

